{title: 226 Buscad primero}
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{lyricist: Karen Lafferty (1948-; Vers. esp.: Anónimo}
{composer: Karen Lafferty (1948- )}

{sov}
1. [D]Buscad primero [A]el [Bm]reino de [F#m]Dios
y [G]su perfecta [D]justicia;[Em][A]
y [D]lo demás [A]añadido [Bm]será. [F#m]Ale[G]lu, [D]alelu[A]ya.[D]

2. [D]No solo de [A]pan el [Bm]hombre vivirá,[F#m]
sino [G]de toda [D]palabra[Em][A]
que [D]sale de [A]la boca [Bm]de Dios. [F#m]Ale[G]lu, [D]alelu[A]ya.[D]

3. [D]Pedid, pe[A]did, y [Bm]se os dará;[F#m]
bus[G]cad, buscad, [D]y hallaréis;[Em][A]
lla[D]mad, lla[A]mad, y se [Bm]os abrirá. [F#m]Ale[G]lu, [D]alelu[A]ya.[D]
{eov}
